Content Insights<br>
1. When web server software runs on web server hardware, and the system is maintained by a company that will sell you some space on it, that is referred to as a web host or hosting.<br>
2. The web client in the context of a web server refers to the device in front of the user that runs web server software to connect to the web server at the request of the user.<br>
3. The Internet was designed to be decentralized. When your files are stored in a cloud, it means that they are stored on a server somewhere.<br>
4. Native Apps are designed for specific OSs. It is coded using programming languages that require compiling. They are usually more expensive to build.<br>
5. Web Apps are cheaper to build and maintain, accessible to everyone within a web browser. They don’t work offline. No one checks web apps’ security issues.<br>
6. The browser manufacturers follow the World Wide Web Consortium (W3C) specifications.<br>
7. Web apps cannot access any of the hardware on the device where they are running. Native apps have the advantage of accessing hardware on the device where they are located. <be>
